---
title: Persisted subagents
id: subagents-persisted
order: 6
description: "Keep the blog desk after a refresh. Subagent cards come back, and a live run continues."
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finish the "},{"type":"link","href":"./subagents","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Subagents"}]},{"type":"text","value":" tutorial first. A refresh on that desk drops every card."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page saves the thread on the server. A closed tab leaves the run in progress. A refresh shows the cards again. If a run is still in progress, the same run continues."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The copy in this tutorial lives in the dev server process. If you restart that process, the chat is gone. A database that saves the same fields keeps the chat."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-install-the-persistence-package","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Install the persistence package"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You already have "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-react"},{"type":"text","value":". Add the store package."}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-keep-one-thread-id","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Keep one thread id"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/lib/thread.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const THREAD_ID = 'blog-desk'","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this same id on the client and on the server. A new id on each load starts an empty chat."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This example has no login, so every visitor shares the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blog-desk"},{"type":"text","value":" thread. In a real app, make sure that the caller owns the thread before POST or GET reads or writes it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-tell-the-hook-that-the-server-owns-the-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Tell the hook that the server owns the chat"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/chat-ui.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":", replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" with this object."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep the message component, the input, and the text part. Step 5 replaces the researcher card."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the layout, set the heading to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Saved blog desk"},{"type":"text","value":". Under that heading, add two sentences. A refresh keeps this chat. A refresh during a run continues the stream."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { blogAgents } from '@/lib/blog-agents'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\nimport { THREAD_ID } from '@/lib/thread'\n\nexport const chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  byok,\n  threadId: THREAD_ID,\n  persistence: true,\n  subagents: blogAgents,\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: true"},{"type":"text","value":" does two things when the page opens."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET ?threadId=blog-desk"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The response is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ messages, activeRun }"},{"type":"text","value":". The hook shows "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"activeRun"},{"type":"text","value":" is set, the hook joins that run. It sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET ?offset=-1&runId="},{"type":"text","value":" and plays the log. The cards continue from that log."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The next load reads the server copy."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"4-replace-the-chat-route","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Replace the chat route"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/routes/api.chat.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" with this file. It is the full route from the example."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  decide,\n  memoryStream,\n  resumeServerSentEventsResponse,\n  subagentRoute,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport {\n  memoryPersistence,\n  reconstructChat,\n  withPersistence,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport {\n  createOpenRouterDecider,\n  createOpenRouterText,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\nimport { createBlogAgents } from '@/lib/agents'\n\nconst FIRST_CHUNK_MS = 30_000\n\nconst persistence = memoryPersistence()\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/chat')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n        const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openrouterByok.id)\n        if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openrouterByok)\n        const agents = createBlogAgents(apiKey)\n        const stream = chat({\n          adapter: createOpenRouterText('openai/gpt-5.5', apiKey),\n          messages: params.messages,\n          threadId: params.threadId,\n          runId: params.runId,\n          middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)],\n          ...(params.parentRunId !== undefined\n            ? { parentRunId: params.parentRunId }\n            : {}),\n          ...(params.resume !== undefined ? { resume: params.resume } : {}),\n          subagents: {\n            agents,\n            strategy: 'exclusive',\n            router: async ({ messages, agents: routed, abortSignal }) => {\n              const state = messages.at(-1)\n              if (state === undefined) return 'main'\n              const route = subagentRoute(routed, { then: ['writer'] })\n              const result = await decide({\n                adapter: createOpenRouterDecider(\n                  '~typesafe/jev-latest',\n                  apiKey,\n                ),\n                state,\n                questions: route.questions,\n                abortSignal,\n              })\n              return route.pick(result)\n            },\n          },\n        })\n        return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, {\n          durability: { adapter: memoryStream(request) },\n        })\n      },\n      GET: ({ request }) => {\n        const durability = memoryStream(request, {\n          firstChunkDeadlineMs: FIRST_CHUNK_MS,\n        })\n        if (durability.resumeFrom() !== null) {\n          return resumeServerSentEventsResponse({ adapter: durability })\n        }\n        return reconstructChat(persistence, request)\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One module-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryPersistence()"},{"type":"text","value":" is the store for every request. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"POST"},{"type":"text","value":" starts a run. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET"},{"type":"text","value":" either replays a live run or rebuilds the saved thread."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"what-the-store-keeps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What the store keeps"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":" writes two kinds of rows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The message store holds the transcript for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blog-desk"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"saveThread"},{"type":"text","value":" replaces that transcript."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The run store holds one row per run."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The parent row uses the chat "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":" and the thread id "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blog-desk"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A child row stores the card id from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SUBAGENT_STARTED"},{"type":"text","value":" as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":" and as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subagentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":" is the chat run. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"researcher"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"writer"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"seo"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The child thread id is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subagent:"},{"type":"text","value":" plus that card id. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"findActiveRun('blog-desk')"},{"type":"text","value":" returns the parent run. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.runId"},{"type":"text","value":" in the child "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" is the parent run id, a colon, and the card id. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.threadId"},{"type":"text","value":" is the parent thread id, a colon, and the agent name."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The middleware saves the child transcript on the child thread: text, reasoning, tool calls, and tool results."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The parent assistant message id is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"assistant:"},{"type":"text","value":" plus the parent run id. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack.runId"},{"type":"text","value":" is that same id. The saved text is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"researcher:"},{"type":"text","value":" and the notes, then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"seo:"},{"type":"text","value":" and the notes."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconstructChat"},{"type":"text","value":" reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.tanstack.runId"},{"type":"text","value":". It calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listByParentRun"},{"type":"text","value":". It puts one card on the assistant message for each child. The card is the only place the notes show."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your own database must save "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subagentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":". It must implement "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listByParentRun"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconstructChat"},{"type":"text","value":" uses that method to build the cards."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"what-post-does","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What POST does"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatParamsFromRequest"},{"type":"text","value":" reads the body. The body has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":". The client also sends the run id in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"X-Run-Id"},{"type":"text","value":" header. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryStream(request)"},{"type":"text","value":" reads that header and opens the log for this run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getByokKey"},{"type":"text","value":" reads the OpenRouter key from the header that the page sends. The call passes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openrouterByok.id"},{"type":"text","value":", so the server does not read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENROUTER_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":". This example has no login, so a server key would pay for requests from any caller."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryStorage()"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the key in memory only. After a refresh, the cards come back without a key. Paste the key again before you send the next message."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" receives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)]"},{"type":"text","value":". On this path the router runs before the main model. The persistence middleware records the child events."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It opens the parent run and saves the messages from the request."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a child starts, it opens the child run and saves the link fields."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a child streams, it saves its text, reasoning, and tool calls."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the turn ends, it marks the parent run and the child runs complete."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsResponse"},{"type":"text","value":" does the delivery."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It writes a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run.accepted"},{"type":"text","value":" chunk into the log before it pulls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":". A refresh during the router can join."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It records every chunk, then sends that chunk to the browser."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the browser disconnects, the helper continues to read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" and writes each chunk into the log. The model continues."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the run ends, it closes the log."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat.stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" stops the view in this tab. The server run continues. A refresh joins it again."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"what-get-does","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What GET does"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryStream(request)"},{"type":"text","value":" looks at the URL."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the URL has a resume offset, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumeFrom()"},{"type":"text","value":" is not null. That request is a join. When the offset is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumeServerSentEventsResponse"},{"type":"text","value":" replays the log from the start. The hook uses that replay to continue a live run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If there is no resume offset, the request is a normal load. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconstructChat(persistence, request)"},{"type":"text","value":" reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"?threadId="},{"type":"text","value":". It returns the saved messages and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"activeRun"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"activeRun"},{"type":"text","value":" is the parent run while its status is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"running"},{"type":"text","value":". After the run is complete, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"activeRun"},{"type":"text","value":" is null. When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"activeRun"},{"type":"text","value":" is null, the hook shows the cards from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"what-the-next-message-sends","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What the next message sends"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook sends the full thread on the next POST. Each card becomes text in the shape "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name:"},{"type":"text","value":" plus the notes. The writer system prompt tells the model to use earlier research text. The writer receives the saved notes in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"5-give-the-researcher-a-tool-and-reasoning","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Give the researcher a tool and reasoning"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A refresh must bring back more than text. Give the researcher one tool and turn on reasoning. Then its card has reasoning, a tool call, and a tool result to restore."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/lib/blog-agents.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolDefinition"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":". Define the tool, then add it to the researcher's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const lookupWikipedia = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'lookupWikipedia',\n  description:\n    'Get the Wikipedia summary of one topic. Pass a short page title, for example \"Octopus\".',\n  inputSchema: {\n    type: 'object',\n    properties: { title: { type: 'string' } },\n    required: ['title'],\n  },\n})\n\nexport const researcher = {\n  name: 'researcher',\n  description:\n    'Does this turn need facts or sources? Answer yes when the user asks to look something up, even if they also ask for a draft or for SEO. Answer no when they do not ask to look anything up.',\n  tools: [lookupWikipedia],\n} as const","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The definition holds no server code, so the browser reads it too. It types the researcher's tool calls in the UI."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/lib/agents.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lookupWikipedia"},{"type":"text","value":" and add the server side of the tool above "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createBlogAgents"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const lookupWikipediaTool = lookupWikipedia.server(async (input) => {\n  const title =\n    typeof input === 'object' &&\n    input !== null &&\n    'title' in input &&\n    typeof input.title === 'string'\n      ? input.title\n      : ''\n  if (title.length === 0) {\n    throw new Error('lookupWikipedia needs a page title')\n  }\n  const response = await fetch(\n    `https://en.wikipedia.org/api/rest_v1/page/summary/${encodeURIComponent(title)}`,\n    { headers: { 'user-agent': 'tanstack-ai-subagents-persisted-example' } },\n  )\n  if (response.status === 404) return { title, found: false }\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error(`Wikipedia returned ${response.status} for ${title}`)\n  }\n  const page: unknown = await response.json()\n  const extract =\n    typeof page === 'object' &&\n    page !== null &&\n    'extract' in page &&\n    typeof page.extract === 'string'\n      ? page.extract\n      : ''\n  if (extract.length === 0) return { title, found: false }\n  return {\n    title,\n    found: true,\n    extract,\n    url: `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/${encodeURIComponent(title)}`,\n  }\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A 404, or a page with no summary, returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ found: false }"},{"type":"text","value":". Any other HTTP status throws, so the card shows the error."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the researcher "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call, add the tool and the reasoning option. Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subagentRunId: ctx.subagentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":" on each child "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":". Tell the model to use the tool:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"modelOptions: { reasoning: { effort: 'medium' } },\ntools: [lookupWikipediaTool],\nsystemPrompts: [\n  'You research for a blog desk. Call lookupWikipedia once for each topic before you reply. Then reply in Markdown with short notes, and give the Wikipedia URL as the source. Use a list. Do not write the full post.',\n],","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/chat-ui.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":", import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingPart"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-react/ui"},{"type":"text","value":". Add a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"thinking"},{"type":"text","value":" entry to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"thinking: ({ part }) => (\n  <ThinkingPart\n    content={part.content}\n    className=\"mb-2 rounded border border-gray-700 bg-gray-800/60 p-2 text-xs text-gray-400\"\n  />\n),","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The researcher card draws the tool call. In "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/components/subagent-card.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":", import the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SubagentPartsProps"},{"type":"text","value":" type from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-react/ui"},{"type":"text","value":". Add the tool widget above the cards:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const researcherTools: SubagentPartsProps<\n  BlogChatOptions,\n  'researcher'\n>['toolsComponents'] = {\n  lookupWikipedia: ({ part, result }) => (\n    <details className=\"mb-2 rounded border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 p-2 text-xs text-emerald-300\">\n      <summary className=\"cursor-pointer font-mono\">\n        lookupWikipedia({part.arguments}) ({part.state})\n      </summary>\n      <pre className=\"mt-1 whitespace-pre-wrap text-gray-400\">\n        {result === undefined\n          ? 'No result yet'\n          : typeof result.content === 'string'\n            ? result.content\n            : JSON.stringify(result.content)}\n      </pre>\n    </details>\n  ),\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace the researcher card with this function. The notes stay open, so the tool row is visible:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export function Researcher({\n  subagent,\n  Parts,\n}: SubagentProps<BlogChatOptions, 'researcher'>) {\n  return (\n    <section className=\"mt-3 rounded-lg border border-orange-500/30 bg-gray-900/80 p-3 text-gray-100\">\n      <AgentHeader\n        name={subagent.name}\n        status={subagent.status}\n        onStop={subagent.stop}\n      />\n      {subagent.error ? (\n        <p className=\"text-xs text-red-400\">{subagent.error.message}</p>\n      ) : null}\n      <div className=\"mt-2\">\n        <Parts toolsComponents={researcherTools} />\n      </div>\n    </section>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The keys come from the researcher's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":". A tool name that the researcher does not have is a type error."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The kit renders a tool call only through a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":" entry with the same name. A tool with no entry renders nothing."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This entry is on the researcher card, so only that card uses it. Its text and reasoning still use the root widgets."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"},{"type":"text","value":" is the matching tool result, so the result shows inside the same row."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To replace other widgets on one card, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../chat/subagents#style-one-childs-parts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Style one child's parts"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"try-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Try it"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paste an OpenRouter key. Send "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"do research on octopuses and seo titles"},{"type":"text","value":". Wait until both cards say finished. The research card shows reasoning, a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lookupWikipedia"},{"type":"text","value":" row, and the notes."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refresh the page. The research card and the SEO card are still there. The research card still has its reasoning and its tool row."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Now write the article"},{"type":"text","value":". The writer uses the saved notes. Refresh. All three cards stay."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send a longer prompt. Refresh while a card says running. The same card continues."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Click Stop while a card says running. Refresh. The same card continues."}]}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"client-example","attributes":{"library":"ai","framework":"react","slug":"subagents-persisted"},"children":[]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-install-the-persistence-package","text":"1. Install the persistence package","level":2},{"id":"2-keep-one-thread-id","text":"2. Keep one thread id","level":2},{"id":"3-tell-the-hook-that-the-server-owns-the-chat","text":"3. Tell the hook that the server owns the chat","level":2},{"id":"4-replace-the-chat-route","text":"4. Replace the chat route","level":2},{"id":"what-the-store-keeps","text":"What the store keeps","level":3},{"id":"what-post-does","text":"What POST does","level":3},{"id":"what-get-does","text":"What GET does","level":3},{"id":"what-the-next-message-sends","text":"What the next message sends","level":3},{"id":"5-give-the-researcher-a-tool-and-reasoning","text":"5. Give the researcher a tool and reasoning","level":2},{"id":"try-it","text":"Try it","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nFinish the [Subagents](./subagents) tutorial first. A refresh on that desk drops every card.\n\nThis page saves the thread on the server. A closed tab leaves the run in progress. A refresh shows the cards again. If a run is still in progress, the same run continues.\n\nThe copy in this tutorial lives in the dev server process. If you restart that process, the chat is gone. A database that saves the same fields keeps the chat.\n\n## 1. Install the persistence package\n\nYou already have `@tanstack/ai` and `@tanstack/ai-react`. Add the store package.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-persistence\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## 2. Keep one thread id\n\nCreate `src/lib/thread.ts`.\n\n```typescript\nexport const THREAD_ID = 'blog-desk'\n```\n\nUse this same id on the client and on the server. A new id on each load starts an empty chat.\n\nThis example has no login, so every visitor shares the `blog-desk` thread. In a real app, make sure that the caller owns the thread before POST or GET reads or writes it.\n\n## 3. Tell the hook that the server owns the chat\n\nIn `src/chat-ui.tsx`, replace `chatOptions` with this object.\n\nKeep the message component, the input, and the text part. Step 5 replaces the researcher card.\n\nIn the layout, set the heading to `Saved blog desk`. Under that heading, add two sentences. A refresh keeps this chat. A refresh during a run continues the stream.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { blogAgents } from '@/lib/blog-agents'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\nimport { THREAD_ID } from '@/lib/thread'\n\nexport const chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  byok,\n  threadId: THREAD_ID,\n  persistence: true,\n  subagents: blogAgents,\n}\n```\n\n`persistence: true` does two things when the page opens.\n\n1. The hook sends `GET ?threadId=blog-desk`.\n2. The response is `{ messages, activeRun }`. The hook shows `messages`.\n\nIf `activeRun` is set, the hook joins that run. It sends `GET ?offset=-1&runId=` and plays the log. The cards continue from that log.\n\nThe next load reads the server copy.\n\n## 4. Replace the chat route\n\nReplace `src/routes/api.chat.ts` with this file. It is the full route from the example.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  decide,\n  memoryStream,\n  resumeServerSentEventsResponse,\n  subagentRoute,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport {\n  memoryPersistence,\n  reconstructChat,\n  withPersistence,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport {\n  createOpenRouterDecider,\n  createOpenRouterText,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\nimport { createBlogAgents } from '@/lib/agents'\n\nconst FIRST_CHUNK_MS = 30_000\n\nconst persistence = memoryPersistence()\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/chat')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n        const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openrouterByok.id)\n        if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openrouterByok)\n        const agents = createBlogAgents(apiKey)\n        const stream = chat({\n          adapter: createOpenRouterText('openai/gpt-5.5', apiKey),\n          messages: params.messages,\n          threadId: params.threadId,\n          runId: params.runId,\n          middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)],\n          ...(params.parentRunId !== undefined\n            ? { parentRunId: params.parentRunId }\n            : {}),\n          ...(params.resume !== undefined ? { resume: params.resume } : {}),\n          subagents: {\n            agents,\n            strategy: 'exclusive',\n            router: async ({ messages, agents: routed, abortSignal }) => {\n              const state = messages.at(-1)\n              if (state === undefined) return 'main'\n              const route = subagentRoute(routed, { then: ['writer'] })\n              const result = await decide({\n                adapter: createOpenRouterDecider(\n                  '~typesafe/jev-latest',\n                  apiKey,\n                ),\n                state,\n                questions: route.questions,\n                abortSignal,\n              })\n              return route.pick(result)\n            },\n          },\n        })\n        return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, {\n          durability: { adapter: memoryStream(request) },\n        })\n      },\n      GET: ({ request }) => {\n        const durability = memoryStream(request, {\n          firstChunkDeadlineMs: FIRST_CHUNK_MS,\n        })\n        if (durability.resumeFrom() !== null) {\n          return resumeServerSentEventsResponse({ adapter: durability })\n        }\n        return reconstructChat(persistence, request)\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nOne module-level `memoryPersistence()` is the store for every request. `POST` starts a run. `GET` either replays a live run or rebuilds the saved thread.\n\n### What the store keeps\n\n`withPersistence` writes two kinds of rows.\n\nThe message store holds the transcript for `blog-desk`. `saveThread` replaces that transcript.\n\nThe run store holds one row per run.\n\n- The parent row uses the chat `runId` and the thread id `blog-desk`.\n- A child row stores the card id from `SUBAGENT_STARTED` as `runId` and as `subagentRunId`. `parentRunId` is the chat run. `name` is `researcher`, `writer`, or `seo`.\n- The child thread id is `subagent:` plus that card id. `findActiveRun('blog-desk')` returns the parent run. `ctx.runId` in the child `chat()` is the parent run id, a colon, and the card id. `ctx.threadId` is the parent thread id, a colon, and the agent name.\n- The middleware saves the child transcript on the child thread: text, reasoning, tool calls, and tool results.\n- The parent assistant message id is `assistant:` plus the parent run id. `metadata.tanstack.runId` is that same id. The saved text is `researcher:` and the notes, then `seo:` and the notes.\n\n`reconstructChat` reads `metadata.tanstack.runId`. It calls `listByParentRun`. It puts one card on the assistant message for each child. The card is the only place the notes show.\n\nYour own database must save `parentRunId`, `subagentRunId`, and `name`. It must implement `listByParentRun`. `reconstructChat` uses that method to build the cards.\n\n### What POST does\n\n`chatParamsFromRequest` reads the body. The body has `messages`, `threadId`, and `runId`. The client also sends the run id in the `X-Run-Id` header. `memoryStream(request)` reads that header and opens the log for this run.\n\n`getByokKey` reads the OpenRouter key from the header that the page sends. The call passes `openrouterByok.id`, so the server does not read `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`. This example has no login, so a server key would pay for requests from any caller.\n\n`memoryStorage()` keeps the key in memory only. After a refresh, the cards come back without a key. Paste the key again before you send the next message.\n\n`chat()` receives `middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)]`. On this path the router runs before the main model. The persistence middleware records the child events.\n\n1. It opens the parent run and saves the messages from the request.\n2. When a child starts, it opens the child run and saves the link fields.\n3. When a child streams, it saves its text, reasoning, and tool calls.\n4. When the turn ends, it marks the parent run and the child runs complete.\n\n`toServerSentEventsResponse` does the delivery.\n\n- It writes a `run.accepted` chunk into the log before it pulls `chat()`. A refresh during the router can join.\n- It records every chunk, then sends that chunk to the browser.\n- If the browser disconnects, the helper continues to read `chat()` and writes each chunk into the log. The model continues.\n- When the run ends, it closes the log.\n\n`chat.stop()` stops the view in this tab. The server run continues. A refresh joins it again.\n\n### What GET does\n\n`memoryStream(request)` looks at the URL.\n\nIf the URL has a resume offset, `resumeFrom()` is not null. That request is a join. When the offset is `-1`, `resumeServerSentEventsResponse` replays the log from the start. The hook uses that replay to continue a live run.\n\nIf there is no resume offset, the request is a normal load. `reconstructChat(persistence, request)` reads `?threadId=`. It returns the saved messages and `activeRun`.\n\n`activeRun` is the parent run while its status is `running`. After the run is complete, `activeRun` is null. When `activeRun` is null, the hook shows the cards from `messages`.\n\n### What the next message sends\n\nThe hook sends the full thread on the next POST. Each card becomes text in the shape `name:` plus the notes. The writer system prompt tells the model to use earlier research text. The writer receives the saved notes in `messages`.\n\n## 5. Give the researcher a tool and reasoning\n\nA refresh must bring back more than text. Give the researcher one tool and turn on reasoning. Then its card has reasoning, a tool call, and a tool result to restore.\n\nIn `src/lib/blog-agents.ts`, add `toolDefinition` from `@tanstack/ai`. Define the tool, then add it to the researcher's `tools`:\n\n```ts ignore\nexport const lookupWikipedia = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'lookupWikipedia',\n  description:\n    'Get the Wikipedia summary of one topic. Pass a short page title, for example \"Octopus\".',\n  inputSchema: {\n    type: 'object',\n    properties: { title: { type: 'string' } },\n    required: ['title'],\n  },\n})\n\nexport const researcher = {\n  name: 'researcher',\n  description:\n    'Does this turn need facts or sources? Answer yes when the user asks to look something up, even if they also ask for a draft or for SEO. Answer no when they do not ask to look anything up.',\n  tools: [lookupWikipedia],\n} as const\n```\n\nThe definition holds no server code, so the browser reads it too. It types the researcher's tool calls in the UI.\n\nIn `src/lib/agents.ts`, import `lookupWikipedia` and add the server side of the tool above `createBlogAgents`:\n\n```ts ignore\nconst lookupWikipediaTool = lookupWikipedia.server(async (input) => {\n  const title =\n    typeof input === 'object' &&\n    input !== null &&\n    'title' in input &&\n    typeof input.title === 'string'\n      ? input.title\n      : ''\n  if (title.length === 0) {\n    throw new Error('lookupWikipedia needs a page title')\n  }\n  const response = await fetch(\n    `https://en.wikipedia.org/api/rest_v1/page/summary/${encodeURIComponent(title)}`,\n    { headers: { 'user-agent': 'tanstack-ai-subagents-persisted-example' } },\n  )\n  if (response.status === 404) return { title, found: false }\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error(`Wikipedia returned ${response.status} for ${title}`)\n  }\n  const page: unknown = await response.json()\n  const extract =\n    typeof page === 'object' &&\n    page !== null &&\n    'extract' in page &&\n    typeof page.extract === 'string'\n      ? page.extract\n      : ''\n  if (extract.length === 0) return { title, found: false }\n  return {\n    title,\n    found: true,\n    extract,\n    url: `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/${encodeURIComponent(title)}`,\n  }\n})\n```\n\nA 404, or a page with no summary, returns `{ found: false }`. Any other HTTP status throws, so the card shows the error.\n\nIn the researcher `chat()` call, add the tool and the reasoning option. Keep `subagentRunId: ctx.subagentRunId` on each child `chat()`. Tell the model to use the tool:\n\n```ts ignore\nmodelOptions: { reasoning: { effort: 'medium' } },\ntools: [lookupWikipediaTool],\nsystemPrompts: [\n  'You research for a blog desk. Call lookupWikipedia once for each topic before you reply. Then reply in Markdown with short notes, and give the Wikipedia URL as the source. Use a list. Do not write the full post.',\n],\n```\n\nIn `src/chat-ui.tsx`, import `ThinkingPart` from `@tanstack/ai-react/ui`. Add a `thinking` entry to `partsComponents`:\n\n```tsx ignore\nthinking: ({ part }) => (\n  <ThinkingPart\n    content={part.content}\n    className=\"mb-2 rounded border border-gray-700 bg-gray-800/60 p-2 text-xs text-gray-400\"\n  />\n),\n```\n\nThe researcher card draws the tool call. In `src/components/subagent-card.tsx`, import the `SubagentPartsProps` type from `@tanstack/ai-react/ui`. Add the tool widget above the cards:\n\n```tsx ignore\nconst researcherTools: SubagentPartsProps<\n  BlogChatOptions,\n  'researcher'\n>['toolsComponents'] = {\n  lookupWikipedia: ({ part, result }) => (\n    <details className=\"mb-2 rounded border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 p-2 text-xs text-emerald-300\">\n      <summary className=\"cursor-pointer font-mono\">\n        lookupWikipedia({part.arguments}) ({part.state})\n      </summary>\n      <pre className=\"mt-1 whitespace-pre-wrap text-gray-400\">\n        {result === undefined\n          ? 'No result yet'\n          : typeof result.content === 'string'\n            ? result.content\n            : JSON.stringify(result.content)}\n      </pre>\n    </details>\n  ),\n}\n```\n\nReplace the researcher card with this function. The notes stay open, so the tool row is visible:\n\n```tsx ignore\nexport function Researcher({\n  subagent,\n  Parts,\n}: SubagentProps<BlogChatOptions, 'researcher'>) {\n  return (\n    <section className=\"mt-3 rounded-lg border border-orange-500/30 bg-gray-900/80 p-3 text-gray-100\">\n      <AgentHeader\n        name={subagent.name}\n        status={subagent.status}\n        onStop={subagent.stop}\n      />\n      {subagent.error ? (\n        <p className=\"text-xs text-red-400\">{subagent.error.message}</p>\n      ) : null}\n      <div className=\"mt-2\">\n        <Parts toolsComponents={researcherTools} />\n      </div>\n    </section>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n- The keys come from the researcher's `tools`. A tool name that the researcher does not have is a type error.\n- The kit renders a tool call only through a `toolsComponents` entry with the same name. A tool with no entry renders nothing.\n- This entry is on the researcher card, so only that card uses it. Its text and reasoning still use the root widgets.\n- `result` is the matching tool result, so the result shows inside the same row.\n\nTo replace other widgets on one card, see [Style one child's parts](../chat/subagents#style-one-childs-parts).\n\n## Try it\n\n1. Paste an OpenRouter key. Send `do research on octopuses and seo titles`. Wait until both cards say finished. The research card shows reasoning, a `lookupWikipedia` row, and the notes.\n2. Refresh the page. The research card and the SEO card are still there. The research card still has its reasoning and its tool row.\n3. Send `Now write the article`. The writer uses the saved notes. Refresh. All three cards stay.\n4. Send a longer prompt. Refresh while a card says running. The same card continues.\n5. Click Stop while a card says running. Refresh. The same card continues.\n\n<!-- ::client-example library=ai framework=react slug=subagents-persisted -->\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Persisted subagents\nid: subagents-persisted\norder: 6\ndescription: \"Keep the blog desk after a refresh. Subagent cards come back, and a live run continues.\"\n---\n\nFinish the [Subagents](./subagents) tutorial first. A refresh on that desk drops every card.\n\nThis page saves the thread on the server. A closed tab leaves the run in progress. A refresh shows the cards again. If a run is still in progress, the same run continues.\n\nThe copy in this tutorial lives in the dev server process. If you restart that process, the chat is gone. A database that saves the same fields keeps the chat.\n\n## 1. Install the persistence package\n\nYou already have `@tanstack/ai` and `@tanstack/ai-react`. Add the store package.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-persistence\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## 2. Keep one thread id\n\nCreate `src/lib/thread.ts`.\n\n```typescript\nexport const THREAD_ID = 'blog-desk'\n```\n\nUse this same id on the client and on the server. A new id on each load starts an empty chat.\n\nThis example has no login, so every visitor shares the `blog-desk` thread. In a real app, make sure that the caller owns the thread before POST or GET reads or writes it.\n\n## 3. Tell the hook that the server owns the chat\n\nIn `src/chat-ui.tsx`, replace `chatOptions` with this object.\n\nKeep the message component, the input, and the text part. Step 5 replaces the researcher card.\n\nIn the layout, set the heading to `Saved blog desk`. Under that heading, add two sentences. A refresh keeps this chat. A refresh during a run continues the stream.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { blogAgents } from '@/lib/blog-agents'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\nimport { THREAD_ID } from '@/lib/thread'\n\nexport const chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  byok,\n  threadId: THREAD_ID,\n  persistence: true,\n  subagents: blogAgents,\n}\n```\n\n`persistence: true` does two things when the page opens.\n\n1. The hook sends `GET ?threadId=blog-desk`.\n2. The response is `{ messages, activeRun }`. The hook shows `messages`.\n\nIf `activeRun` is set, the hook joins that run. It sends `GET ?offset=-1&runId=` and plays the log. The cards continue from that log.\n\nThe next load reads the server copy.\n\n## 4. Replace the chat route\n\nReplace `src/routes/api.chat.ts` with this file. It is the full route from the example.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  decide,\n  memoryStream,\n  resumeServerSentEventsResponse,\n  subagentRoute,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport {\n  memoryPersistence,\n  reconstructChat,\n  withPersistence,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport {\n  createOpenRouterDecider,\n  createOpenRouterText,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\nimport { createBlogAgents } from '@/lib/agents'\n\nconst FIRST_CHUNK_MS = 30_000\n\nconst persistence = memoryPersistence()\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/chat')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n        const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openrouterByok.id)\n        if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openrouterByok)\n        const agents = createBlogAgents(apiKey)\n        const stream = chat({\n          adapter: createOpenRouterText('openai/gpt-5.5', apiKey),\n          messages: params.messages,\n          threadId: params.threadId,\n          runId: params.runId,\n          middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)],\n          ...(params.parentRunId !== undefined\n            ? { parentRunId: params.parentRunId }\n            : {}),\n          ...(params.resume !== undefined ? { resume: params.resume } : {}),\n          subagents: {\n            agents,\n            strategy: 'exclusive',\n            router: async ({ messages, agents: routed, abortSignal }) => {\n              const state = messages.at(-1)\n              if (state === undefined) return 'main'\n              const route = subagentRoute(routed, { then: ['writer'] })\n              const result = await decide({\n                adapter: createOpenRouterDecider(\n                  '~typesafe/jev-latest',\n                  apiKey,\n                ),\n                state,\n                questions: route.questions,\n                abortSignal,\n              })\n              return route.pick(result)\n            },\n          },\n        })\n        return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, {\n          durability: { adapter: memoryStream(request) },\n        })\n      },\n      GET: ({ request }) => {\n        const durability = memoryStream(request, {\n          firstChunkDeadlineMs: FIRST_CHUNK_MS,\n        })\n        if (durability.resumeFrom() !== null) {\n          return resumeServerSentEventsResponse({ adapter: durability })\n        }\n        return reconstructChat(persistence, request)\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nOne module-level `memoryPersistence()` is the store for every request. `POST` starts a run. `GET` either replays a live run or rebuilds the saved thread.\n\n### What the store keeps\n\n`withPersistence` writes two kinds of rows.\n\nThe message store holds the transcript for `blog-desk`. `saveThread` replaces that transcript.\n\nThe run store holds one row per run.\n\n- The parent row uses the chat `runId` and the thread id `blog-desk`.\n- A child row stores the card id from `SUBAGENT_STARTED` as `runId` and as `subagentRunId`. `parentRunId` is the chat run. `name` is `researcher`, `writer`, or `seo`.\n- The child thread id is `subagent:` plus that card id. `findActiveRun('blog-desk')` returns the parent run. `ctx.runId` in the child `chat()` is the parent run id, a colon, and the card id. `ctx.threadId` is the parent thread id, a colon, and the agent name.\n- The middleware saves the child transcript on the child thread: text, reasoning, tool calls, and tool results.\n- The parent assistant message id is `assistant:` plus the parent run id. `metadata.tanstack.runId` is that same id. The saved text is `researcher:` and the notes, then `seo:` and the notes.\n\n`reconstructChat` reads `metadata.tanstack.runId`. It calls `listByParentRun`. It puts one card on the assistant message for each child. The card is the only place the notes show.\n\nYour own database must save `parentRunId`, `subagentRunId`, and `name`. It must implement `listByParentRun`. `reconstructChat` uses that method to build the cards.\n\n### What POST does\n\n`chatParamsFromRequest` reads the body. The body has `messages`, `threadId`, and `runId`. The client also sends the run id in the `X-Run-Id` header. `memoryStream(request)` reads that header and opens the log for this run.\n\n`getByokKey` reads the OpenRouter key from the header that the page sends. The call passes `openrouterByok.id`, so the server does not read `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`. This example has no login, so a server key would pay for requests from any caller.\n\n`memoryStorage()` keeps the key in memory only. After a refresh, the cards come back without a key. Paste the key again before you send the next message.\n\n`chat()` receives `middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)]`. On this path the router runs before the main model. The persistence middleware records the child events.\n\n1. It opens the parent run and saves the messages from the request.\n2. When a child starts, it opens the child run and saves the link fields.\n3. When a child streams, it saves its text, reasoning, and tool calls.\n4. When the turn ends, it marks the parent run and the child runs complete.\n\n`toServerSentEventsResponse` does the delivery.\n\n- It writes a `run.accepted` chunk into the log before it pulls `chat()`. A refresh during the router can join.\n- It records every chunk, then sends that chunk to the browser.\n- If the browser disconnects, the helper continues to read `chat()` and writes each chunk into the log. The model continues.\n- When the run ends, it closes the log.\n\n`chat.stop()` stops the view in this tab. The server run continues. A refresh joins it again.\n\n### What GET does\n\n`memoryStream(request)` looks at the URL.\n\nIf the URL has a resume offset, `resumeFrom()` is not null. That request is a join. When the offset is `-1`, `resumeServerSentEventsResponse` replays the log from the start. The hook uses that replay to continue a live run.\n\nIf there is no resume offset, the request is a normal load. `reconstructChat(persistence, request)` reads `?threadId=`. It returns the saved messages and `activeRun`.\n\n`activeRun` is the parent run while its status is `running`. After the run is complete, `activeRun` is null. When `activeRun` is null, the hook shows the cards from `messages`.\n\n### What the next message sends\n\nThe hook sends the full thread on the next POST. Each card becomes text in the shape `name:` plus the notes. The writer system prompt tells the model to use earlier research text. The writer receives the saved notes in `messages`.\n\n## 5. Give the researcher a tool and reasoning\n\nA refresh must bring back more than text. Give the researcher one tool and turn on reasoning. Then its card has reasoning, a tool call, and a tool result to restore.\n\nIn `src/lib/blog-agents.ts`, add `toolDefinition` from `@tanstack/ai`. Define the tool, then add it to the researcher's `tools`:\n\n```ts ignore\nexport const lookupWikipedia = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'lookupWikipedia',\n  description:\n    'Get the Wikipedia summary of one topic. Pass a short page title, for example \"Octopus\".',\n  inputSchema: {\n    type: 'object',\n    properties: { title: { type: 'string' } },\n    required: ['title'],\n  },\n})\n\nexport const researcher = {\n  name: 'researcher',\n  description:\n    'Does this turn need facts or sources? Answer yes when the user asks to look something up, even if they also ask for a draft or for SEO. Answer no when they do not ask to look anything up.',\n  tools: [lookupWikipedia],\n} as const\n```\n\nThe definition holds no server code, so the browser reads it too. It types the researcher's tool calls in the UI.\n\nIn `src/lib/agents.ts`, import `lookupWikipedia` and add the server side of the tool above `createBlogAgents`:\n\n```ts ignore\nconst lookupWikipediaTool = lookupWikipedia.server(async (input) => {\n  const title =\n    typeof input === 'object' &&\n    input !== null &&\n    'title' in input &&\n    typeof input.title === 'string'\n      ? input.title\n      : ''\n  if (title.length === 0) {\n    throw new Error('lookupWikipedia needs a page title')\n  }\n  const response = await fetch(\n    `https://en.wikipedia.org/api/rest_v1/page/summary/${encodeURIComponent(title)}`,\n    { headers: { 'user-agent': 'tanstack-ai-subagents-persisted-example' } },\n  )\n  if (response.status === 404) return { title, found: false }\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error(`Wikipedia returned ${response.status} for ${title}`)\n  }\n  const page: unknown = await response.json()\n  const extract =\n    typeof page === 'object' &&\n    page !== null &&\n    'extract' in page &&\n    typeof page.extract === 'string'\n      ? page.extract\n      : ''\n  if (extract.length === 0) return { title, found: false }\n  return {\n    title,\n    found: true,\n    extract,\n    url: `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/${encodeURIComponent(title)}`,\n  }\n})\n```\n\nA 404, or a page with no summary, returns `{ found: false }`. Any other HTTP status throws, so the card shows the error.\n\nIn the researcher `chat()` call, add the tool and the reasoning option. Keep `subagentRunId: ctx.subagentRunId` on each child `chat()`. Tell the model to use the tool:\n\n```ts ignore\nmodelOptions: { reasoning: { effort: 'medium' } },\ntools: [lookupWikipediaTool],\nsystemPrompts: [\n  'You research for a blog desk. Call lookupWikipedia once for each topic before you reply. Then reply in Markdown with short notes, and give the Wikipedia URL as the source. Use a list. Do not write the full post.',\n],\n```\n\nIn `src/chat-ui.tsx`, import `ThinkingPart` from `@tanstack/ai-react/ui`. Add a `thinking` entry to `partsComponents`:\n\n```tsx ignore\nthinking: ({ part }) => (\n  <ThinkingPart\n    content={part.content}\n    className=\"mb-2 rounded border border-gray-700 bg-gray-800/60 p-2 text-xs text-gray-400\"\n  />\n),\n```\n\nThe researcher card draws the tool call. In `src/components/subagent-card.tsx`, import the `SubagentPartsProps` type from `@tanstack/ai-react/ui`. Add the tool widget above the cards:\n\n```tsx ignore\nconst researcherTools: SubagentPartsProps<\n  BlogChatOptions,\n  'researcher'\n>['toolsComponents'] = {\n  lookupWikipedia: ({ part, result }) => (\n    <details className=\"mb-2 rounded border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 p-2 text-xs text-emerald-300\">\n      <summary className=\"cursor-pointer font-mono\">\n        lookupWikipedia({part.arguments}) ({part.state})\n      </summary>\n      <pre className=\"mt-1 whitespace-pre-wrap text-gray-400\">\n        {result === undefined\n          ? 'No result yet'\n          : typeof result.content === 'string'\n            ? result.content\n            : JSON.stringify(result.content)}\n      </pre>\n    </details>\n  ),\n}\n```\n\nReplace the researcher card with this function. The notes stay open, so the tool row is visible:\n\n```tsx ignore\nexport function Researcher({\n  subagent,\n  Parts,\n}: SubagentProps<BlogChatOptions, 'researcher'>) {\n  return (\n    <section className=\"mt-3 rounded-lg border border-orange-500/30 bg-gray-900/80 p-3 text-gray-100\">\n      <AgentHeader\n        name={subagent.name}\n        status={subagent.status}\n        onStop={subagent.stop}\n      />\n      {subagent.error ? (\n        <p className=\"text-xs text-red-400\">{subagent.error.message}</p>\n      ) : null}\n      <div className=\"mt-2\">\n        <Parts toolsComponents={researcherTools} />\n      </div>\n    </section>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n- The keys come from the researcher's `tools`. A tool name that the researcher does not have is a type error.\n- The kit renders a tool call only through a `toolsComponents` entry with the same name. A tool with no entry renders nothing.\n- This entry is on the researcher card, so only that card uses it. Its text and reasoning still use the root widgets.\n- `result` is the matching tool result, so the result shows inside the same row.\n\nTo replace other widgets on one card, see [Style one child's parts](../chat/subagents#style-one-childs-parts).\n\n## Try it\n\n1. Paste an OpenRouter key. Send `do research on octopuses and seo titles`. Wait until both cards say finished. The research card shows reasoning, a `lookupWikipedia` row, and the notes.\n2. Refresh the page. The research card and the SEO card are still there. The research card still has its reasoning and its tool row.\n3. Send `Now write the article`. The writer uses the saved notes. Refresh. All three cards stay.\n4. Send a longer prompt. Refresh while a card says running. The same card continues.\n5. Click Stop while a card says running. Refresh. The same card continues.\n\n<!-- ::client-example library=ai framework=react slug=subagents-persisted -->\n"}
